[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":88},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":-7,"_16":17,"_18":19,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25},"tipo","metodo","cubo",{"_11":86,"_13":86,"_27":87},"id","ortega","nome","Ortega","nomeLongo","termo",{"_27":83,"_84":85},"niveis",[46],"introducao","<p>A first fast method: build just the bottom face (without caring about the sides), orient the top one (<a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a> <a href=\"/en/glossary#oll\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Makes the top face all one color, without caring about the position of the pieces. There are 57 cases; in 2-Look OLL, 10 cases in two parts.\">OLL</a>, 7 cases) and permute both layers at once (Ortega <a href=\"/en/glossary#pbl\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 2x2 (Ortega): puts the pieces of both layers in place at once.\">PBL</a>, 6 cases).</p>\n","etapas",[31,32,33],"historias",[26],{"_13":14,"_27":28,"_29":30},"endereco","/historia#ortega","resumo","The method is named after Victor Ortega, who spread it (in 2001 it went up on Josef Jelinek's site), but the idea is older: it comes from a corners-first 3x3 method, published by Jeffrey Varasano in 1981, which is why it is also called the Varasano method.",{"_11":77,"_13":78,"_36":79,"_38":80,"_40":81,"_41":-7},{"_11":60,"_13":61,"_36":62,"_38":63,"_40":-7,"_41":64},{"_11":34,"_13":35,"_36":37,"_38":39,"_40":-7,"_41":42},"pbl","PBL","html","<p>Both faces are done: the corners just need swapping until the sides match. Look at each layer: a side with both colors matching (a &quot;<a href=\"/en/glossary#par\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A corner and an edge that go together into the same slot in F2L.\">pair</a>&quot;) means an adjacent swap (<em>Adj</em>); no pair, a diagonal swap (<em>Opp</em>). A layer that is already right has a pair on all 4 sides. The 6 cases are the combinations of the two layers; if only the bottom one is wrong, turn the cube over (<code>x2</code>) and it goes to the top. At the end, a <code>U</code> or <code>D</code> turn finishes it.</p>\n","grupos",[43],"pagina","treino","/2x2/treino?grupo=ortega-pbl",{"_11":44,"_13":44,"_45":46,"_47":48,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_27":53},"Ortega PBL","nivel","iniciante","casos",6,"conjunto",false,"ids",[54,55,56,57,58,59],"/2x2/ortega-pbl","2X2-PBL-Adj","2X2-PBL-Opp","2X2-PBL-OppOpp","2X2-PBL-AdjAdj","2X2-PBL-AdjOpp","2X2-PBL-OppAdj","oll","OLL","<p>With white on the bottom, make the top face all yellow. Look at how many yellow stickers are already on top and where the others are, on the sides: there are 7 cases, the same shapes as the corners of the 3x3 <a href=\"/en/glossary#oll\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Makes the top face all one color, without caring about the position of the pieces. There are 57 cases; in 2-Look OLL, 10 cases in two parts.\">OLL</a> (<a href=\"/en/glossary#sune\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Two short OLL algorithms that orient 3 corners: R U R' U R U2 R' (Sune) and R U2 R' U' R U' R' (Anti-Sune).\">Sune</a>, AntiSune, H, Pi, P, T and L).</p>\n",[65],"/2x2/treino?grupo=ortega-oll",{"_11":66,"_13":66,"_45":46,"_47":67,"_49":50,"_51":68,"_27":69},"Ortega OLL",7,[70,71,72,73,74,75,76],"/2x2/ortega-oll","2X2-OLL-Sune","2X2-OLL-AntiSune","2X2-OLL-Pi","2X2-OLL-P","2X2-OLL-L","2X2-OLL-T","2X2-OLL-H","primeira-face","1st face","<p>The white face on the bottom, with the <a href=\"/en/glossary#sexy-move\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The trigger R U R' U', the most common of all.\">sexy move</a> <code>R U R&#39; U&#39;</code>. The sides may end up swapped.</p>\n",[],{"_13":78,"_27":82},"/2x2/primeira-face","/en/glossary#ortega","dica","A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).","2x2","/2x2/",{"_89":90,"_91":92},"cubos",[95,96,97,98,99,100],"idiomas",[93,94],"pt","en",{"_11":107,"_13":107},{"_11":86,"_13":86},{"_11":106,"_13":106},{"_11":105,"_13":105},{"_11":103,"_13":104},{"_11":101,"_13":102},"pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
